@startuml Forum_Sequence_01_Registration_OTP
title Forum Platform - Sequence Diagram 01: Registration with OTP (DEC-001 Reconciled)
autonumber
hide footbox
skinparam style strictuml
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

actor Guest
boundary "Web Frontend" as FE
control "API Gateway" as GW
control "User Service" as US
database "User DB" as UDB
queue "Email Provider" as MAIL

Guest -> FE: Enter username, email, password
FE -> GW: POST /auth/register
GW -> US: Forward registration request
US -> UDB: Check username/email uniqueness
UDB --> US: Check result

alt Username or email already registered (DEC-001 Neutral Handling)
  US ->> MAIL: Send notification email ("Account already exists / Reset password link")
  US --> GW: 202 Accepted (Neutral response)
  GW --> FE: 202 Accepted ("If eligible, a verification code has been sent")
  FE --> Guest: Show OTP entry screen with generic guidance
else Username and email available
  US -> US: Hash password\nGenerate OTP and expiry (5 min)
  US -> UDB: Save pending registration + OTP hash
  UDB --> US: Saved
  US ->> MAIL: Send OTP verification email
  MAIL --> US: Accepted / delivery status
  US --> GW: 202 Accepted (Neutral response)
  GW --> FE: 202 Accepted ("If eligible, a verification code has been sent")
  FE --> Guest: Show OTP entry screen
end

Guest -> FE: Enter OTP
FE -> GW: POST /auth/register/verify
GW -> US: Forward OTP verification {email, otp}
US -> UDB: Load pending registration by email
UDB --> US: OTP hash, expiry, attempts, resend count

alt OTP is valid and not expired
  US -> UDB: Create account + consume pending registration
  UDB --> US: Account created
  US --> GW: 201 Created + UserPublic
  GW --> FE: Success
  FE --> Guest: Show registration confirmation / prompt to sign in
else OTP is incorrect
  US -> UDB: Increment failed attempts counter
  US --> GW: 400 Invalid OTP
  GW --> FE: Verification failed
  FE --> Guest: Show OTP error; retain email
else OTP expired or attempt limit reached
  US --> GW: 400 OTP expired or limit exceeded
  GW --> FE: Verification locked
  FE --> Guest: Offer resend OTP or restart registration
end
@enduml

@startuml Forum_Sequence_02_Login_Session
title Forum Platform - Sequence Diagram 02: Login and Session Creation
autonumber
hide footbox
skinparam style strictuml
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

actor "Guest / Member" as User
boundary "Web Frontend" as FE
control "API Gateway" as GW
control "User Service" as US
database "User DB" as UDB
database "Redis / Rate Limiter" as RL

User -> FE: Submit login (username/email) + password
FE -> GW: POST /auth/login
GW -> RL: Check rate limit / failure counters
RL --> GW: Allowed or blocked

alt Rate limit exceeded
  GW --> FE: 429 Too Many Requests
  FE --> User: Show retry guidance / CAPTCHA if required
else Request allowed
  GW -> US: Forward login request
  US -> UDB: Find account by normalized login
  UDB --> US: Account status + password hash

  alt Account missing or password invalid
    US -> RL: Record failed login attempt
    US --> GW: 401 Invalid credentials (generic)
    GW --> FE: Login failed
    FE --> User: Show generic credential error
  else Account is banned
    US --> GW: 403 Account restricted
    GW --> FE: Login denied
    FE --> User: Show ban reason and duration
  else Credentials valid and account active
    US -> US: Generate opaque session token
    US -> UDB: Persist session (idle 4h, absolute 24h)
    UDB --> US: Session saved
    US --> GW: 200 OK + Set-Cookie: forum_session
    GW --> FE: Set-Cookie: HttpOnly; Secure; SameSite=Lax; Path=/
    FE --> User: Navigate to forum dashboard
  end
end
@enduml

@startuml Forum_Sequence_03_Create_Thread
title Forum Platform - Sequence Diagram 03: Create Thread (DEC-003 Reconciled)
autonumber
hide footbox
skinparam style strictuml
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

actor Member
boundary "Web Frontend" as FE
control "API Gateway" as GW
control "User Service" as US
control "Content Service" as CS
database "User DB" as UDB
database "Content DB" as CDB
control "Notification Service" as NS
control "Search Service" as SS
queue "Event Bus / Outbox" as BUS

Member -> FE: Submit title, body, category, tags, optional image_ids
FE -> GW: POST /threads + session cookie + X-CSRF-Token + Idempotency-Key
GW -> US: Validate session and member permissions
US -> UDB: Check session validity and ban status
UDB --> US: Valid member
US --> GW: Auth context (user_id, role)

alt Unauthenticated or restricted
  GW --> FE: 401 / 403
  FE --> Member: Show error
else Authenticated
  GW -> CS: Create thread command
  CS -> CS: Validate title, body, tag limit\nVerify image_ids in attachments table
  CS -> CDB: Insert thread (status='published', is_locked=false, is_pinned=false)\nLink attachments + Write ThreadCreated outbox event
  CDB --> CS: Committed with Thread ID
  CS --> GW: 201 Created + Thread schema
  GW --> FE: Thread created
  FE --> Member: Display new thread

  BUS -> SS: ThreadCreated event
  SS -> SS: Index thread in search documents
  BUS -> NS: ThreadCreated event
  NS -> NS: Notify subscribed category members
end
@enduml

@startuml Forum_Sequence_04_Comment_And_Notification
title Forum Platform - Sequence Diagram 04: Add Comment / Reply
autonumber
hide footbox
skinparam style strictuml
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

actor Member
boundary "Web Frontend" as FE
control "API Gateway" as GW
control "User Service" as US
control "Content Service" as CS
database "Content DB" as CDB
control "Notification Service" as NS
queue "Event Bus / Outbox" as BUS

Member -> FE: Submit comment or reply
FE -> GW: POST /threads/{id}/comments + cookie + CSRF + Idempotency-Key
GW -> US: Validate session
US --> GW: Auth context

alt Authenticated
  GW -> CS: Create comment command
  CS -> CDB: Check thread is open (is_locked=false)\nVerify parent depth (max 2 levels)
  CDB --> CS: Preconditions pass
  CS -> CDB: Insert comment + Write CommentCreated outbox event
  CDB --> CS: Committed
  CS --> GW: 201 Created + Comment schema
  GW --> FE: Comment created
  FE --> Member: Display new comment

  BUS -> NS: CommentCreated event
  NS -> NS: Create in-app notification for thread author / replier
end
@enduml

@startuml Forum_Sequence_05_Vote_BestAnswer
title Forum Platform - Sequence Diagram 05: Vote and Mark Best Answer (DEC-002 Reconciled)
autonumber
hide footbox
skinparam style strictuml
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

actor Member
boundary "Web Frontend" as FE
control "API Gateway" as GW
control "User Service" as US
control "Interaction Service" as IS
control "Content Service" as CS
database "Interaction DB" as IDB
database "User DB" as UDB
database "Content DB" as CDB
queue "Event Bus / Outbox" as BUS

Member -> FE: Click upvote/downvote
FE -> GW: PUT /threads/{id}/vote (or /comments/{id}/vote) + CSRF
GW -> US: Validate session
US --> GW: Auth context (voter_id)

alt Authenticated
  GW -> IS: Submit vote (value: 1 or -1)
  IS -> CS: Internal REST: Get target author and state
  CS --> IS: Target metadata (author_id, is_active)

  alt Self-vote attempted
    IS --> GW: 400 SELF_VOTE_NOT_ALLOWED
    GW --> FE: Error
  else Valid vote
    IS -> IDB: Upsert vote or cancel if same value\nWrite reputation ledger entry + outbox
    IDB --> IS: Committed
    IS --> GW: 200 OK + VoteResponse (score, my_vote, delta)
    GW --> FE: Updated score
    FE --> Member: Reflect vote state

    BUS -> US: ReputationChanged event
    US -> UDB: Update cached user reputation if applicable
  end
end

== Mark Best Answer ==
Member -> FE: Select Best Answer
FE -> GW: PUT /threads/{id}/best-answer + CSRF
GW -> US: Validate session
US --> GW: Auth context
GW -> CS: Set best answer {comment_id}
CS -> CDB: Verify requester is author, category is Q&A, thread not locked
CDB --> CS: Preconditions pass
CS -> CDB: Set best_answer_comment_id + Write BestAnswerChanged outbox event
CDB --> CS: Committed
CS --> GW: 200 OK
GW --> FE: Best answer marked
FE --> Member: Highlight best answer

BUS -> IS: BestAnswerChanged event
IS -> IDB: Award reputation bonus to comment author in ledger
@enduml

@startuml Forum_Sequence_06_Report_Moderation
title Forum Platform - Sequence Diagram 06: Abuse Report and Moderation (DEC-004 Reconciled)
autonumber
hide footbox
skinparam style strictuml
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

actor Member
actor Moderator
boundary "Web Frontend" as FE
control "API Gateway" as GW
control "User Service" as US
control "Moderation Service" as MS
control "Content Service" as CS
database "Moderation DB" as MDB
database "Content DB" as CDB
database "User DB" as UDB
queue "Event Bus / Outbox" as BUS

Member -> FE: Submit report (target: thread/comment/account, reason, details)
FE -> GW: POST /reports + CSRF + Idempotency-Key
GW -> US: Validate session
US --> GW: Auth context (reporter_id)

alt Authenticated
  GW -> MS: Create report
  MS -> MDB: Check active report duplicate for reporter & target
  MDB --> MS: Check result

  alt Already reported
    MS --> GW: 409 DUPLICATE_REPORT
    GW --> FE: Already reported
  else New report
    MS -> MDB: Insert report (status='pending')
    MDB --> MS: Report ID
    MS --> GW: 201 Created + Report schema
    GW --> FE: Confirmation
    FE --> Member: Show submission confirmation
  end
end

== Moderator Resolves Report ==
Moderator -> FE: Review report in queue
FE -> GW: GET /moderation/reports?status=pending
GW -> US: Verify moderator role
US --> GW: Authorized
GW -> MS: Fetch queue
MS -> MDB: Query reports
MDB --> MS: Queue items
MS --> GW: 200 OK
GW --> FE: Display queue

Moderator -> FE: Apply action (e.g. lock_thread, ban_user)
FE -> GW: POST /moderation/reports/{report_id}/actions + CSRF
GW -> MS: Execute moderation action
MS -> MDB: Save action (with report_id) + update report (status='actioned')
MDB --> MS: Committed

alt Content Action (lock/hidden/deleted)
  MS -> CS: Internal REST / Event: Update thread status or is_locked
  CS -> CDB: Apply content update
end

alt Account Action (ban user)
  MS -> US: Internal REST / Event: Ban account and revoke sessions
  US -> UDB: Set is_banned=true, revoke sessions
end

MS -> BUS: ModerationActionApplied event
MS --> GW: 200 OK + ModerationAction schema
GW --> FE: Action completed
FE --> Moderator: Show resolution confirmation
@enduml

@startuml Forum_Sequence_07_Search
title Forum Platform - Sequence Diagram 07: Search Visible Threads
autonumber
hide footbox
skinparam style strictuml
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

actor Visitor
boundary "Web Frontend" as FE
control "API Gateway" as GW
control "Search Service" as SS
database "Search DB" as SDB

Visitor -> FE: Enter search query & filters
FE -> GW: GET /search?q=...&category_id=...&sort=...
GW -> SS: Forward search request
SS -> SS: Validate & normalize query
SS -> SDB: Full-text search with tsvector simple ranking
SDB --> SS: Matching documents
SS --> GW: 200 OK + SearchPage
GW --> FE: Results + next_cursor
FE --> Visitor: Render search results
@enduml

@startuml Forum_Sequence_08_View_Count_Propagation
title Forum Platform - Sequence Diagram 08: View Count Tracking & Propagation (DEC-005)
autonumber
hide footbox
skinparam style strictuml
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

actor Visitor
boundary "Web Frontend" as FE
control "API Gateway" as GW
control "Interaction Service" as IS
database "Interaction DB" as IDB
control "Content Service" as CS
database "Content DB" as CDB
queue "Event Bus / Outbox" as BUS

Visitor -> FE: Open thread page
FE -> GW: POST /threads/{thread_id}/view (Session or IP HMAC)
GW -> IS: Record thread view
IS -> IDB: Check session_key_hash in 30-minute deduplication window
IDB --> IS: Window check result

alt Already viewed in last 30 minutes
  IS --> GW: 204 No Content (Deduplicated)
  GW --> FE: 204 No Content
else First view in window
  IS -> IDB: Insert thread_views record\nWrite ThreadViewCountIncremented to outbox
  IDB --> IS: Committed
  IS --> GW: 204 No Content
  GW --> FE: 204 No Content

  BUS -> CS: ThreadViewCountIncremented event {thread_id, increment: 1}
  CS -> CDB: UPDATE content.threads SET view_count = view_count + 1 WHERE id = thread_id
  CDB --> CS: Updated
end
@enduml
